invariant: INV-71
file: src/sha3.c
catches: sha3_equiv_test
reason: shake_init writes 0 to wipes_below, so every SHAKE context skips the
  wipe of the stack below its calls, the noise and the hashes of ML-KEM
  and ML-DSA-87 too. Every output is still right. bin/sha3_equiv_test,
  a device object's build, starts its contexts with shake128_init and
  shake256_init, copies the stack below each kind of call and finds a
  lane the call computed from its input (docs/decisions.md 236).

--- old
    s->squeezing = 0;
    s->wipes_below = 1;
--- new
    s->squeezing = 0;
    s->wipes_below = 0;
